sequenceDiagram
    participant Handler as Feature Handler
    participant DB as MySQL Transaction
    participant Outbox as Outbox Table
    participant Reader as Outbox Reader Worker
    participant Queue as Internal Queue
    participant Consumer as Idempotent Consumer
    participant Notify as Notifications
    participant Search as Search
    participant Audit as Audit
    participant DeadLetter as Dead-Letter Review

    Note over Handler,Outbox: The Handler that initiated the use case is the transaction owner
    Handler->>DB: BEGIN
    Handler->>DB: Write business state
    Handler->>Outbox: INSERT event<br/>(event_id, type, schema_version, payload, occurred_at)
    Handler->>DB: COMMIT

    Reader->>Outbox: Read committed pending events
    Outbox-->>Reader: Pending events batch
    Reader->>Queue: Dispatch event envelope
    Reader->>Outbox: Record dispatch attempt

    Queue-->>Consumer: Deliver envelope
    Consumer->>Consumer: Lookup event_id in dedupe store
    alt First delivery
        Consumer->>Notify: Create notification
        Consumer->>Search: Index authorized record
        Consumer->>Audit: Append delivery record
        Consumer->>Queue: ACK
    else Duplicate delivery
        Consumer->>Queue: ACK and skip
    end

    Note over Consumer,DeadLetter: On failure, retry with a clear backoff policy.<br/>After the retry threshold the event moves to Dead-Letter for super admin review.<br/>The original transaction is not lost and its result is not repeated.
